east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback is verified, and all three regions are now on v2.3.0.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both marked unhealthy, and the service was failing at a 0.18 error rate on v2.3.1.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure and the rollback, and it paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI did not confirm that the error rate has dropped since the rollback. Someone should check that, and should investigate the v2.3.1 failure before that version is released again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01S4yf3Xvf4Fc6nhqBmZ9jwk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013zq1q74XzHUpTpgm4ZjZDY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1). v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy. Rolling back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01J19xbmxdauFEbHRTmust8i", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RHsgmVoWchFPets9PuwQXr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate was 0.18 in all regions: us-east, us-west, eu-west). Deployment history shows v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are unhealthy; v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. The rollback reports VERIFIED, with all three regions now on v2.3.0. Follow-up: confirm error rate has recovered, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.", "confidence": 0.9, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback is verified, and all three regions are now on v2.3.0.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both marked unhealthy, and the service was failing at a 0.18 error rate on v2.3.1.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure and the rollback, and it paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI did not confirm that the error rate has dropped since the rollback. Someone should check that, and should investigate the v2.3.1 failure before that version is released again.", "type": "text"}]}]}